From: levy@cs.utk.edu
Date: Mon, 5 Dec 1994 19:21:18 -0500
Subject: [#94-12-173] ASTRO: My problem with astrology

It strikes me as very unlikely that evolution would support the
periodicity implied by astrology, because such periodicity could
have catastrophic consequences.  Neural networks screw up when they
get caught in a cycle; bridges collapse when they oscillate too much
(c.f. the "break your stride" command found at the entrance to bridges
under construction), and, in general, complex systems need a certain
amount of chaos to prevent them from being led down a garden path to
destruction.  So I consider it unlikely that all people born in a given
year (or month, or whatver) would have similar characteristics.  I don't
mean to imply that nature "knows" about such things; rather, if nature
_did_ operate in that kind of lockstep, some catastrophe would likely 
have wiped out life eons ago.

-- Simon

